    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="c158d519-39eb-5f79-ac97-ed945b5752c9" activityNameId="d2782c80-2b76-50de-9135-6397121eb8ad" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">OLED screen 43 inches, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: OLED screen 43 inches, at plant
Data are based on information from a recent dismantling study of various consumer electronics; UUID: 43f7e2c2-abd2-3f86-b3e3-c695159f8bb1
The dataset for the OLED screen is assumed to have equivalent the bill of materials as the LED screen monitors, according to the other dismantling studies (source: Babbitt et al., 2020; Peeters et al., 2012). However, the module type is specifically adapted using OLED based modules - which is modeled in a separate dataset. The average size of the modeled OLED monitor is 43 inches, with a total weight of approximately 9.3 kg. The model is based on the actual product LG smart TV 43" 43UH610A-UJ (LG, 2016). The monitor comprises metals (copper, steel), plastics (ABS), PCB, and flat panel glass, whose weight shares are defined from the bill of materials data from Babbitt et al., 2020.
Location: Data from publications &amp; internet survey information, representing averages.
Technology: 43 inch, OLED (backlighting) color screen.
Time period: Unspecified
Production volume: unknown
Sampling: literature &amp; own estimations
Extrapolations: see general comment
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_43f7e2c2-abd2-3f86-b3e3-c695159f8bb1.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
